Red Bandit wrote:
>
> So, I'm XP level 6 on level 4 in the Gnomish Mines. I've just seen the
> most dreaded of all message sequences, "The hill orc puts on a pair of
> hard shoes. The hill orc wields the blessed Dragonsbane."

Vanilla discussion -

Dragonbane hits you no harder than any other broadsword.  If I read
the docs right it doesn't even hit you more often than any other
broadsword.  Being blessed it's at least +0 is the worst I could say.
Unless you are currently polymorphed into a dragon!

Orcs often carry scimitars.  Comparing the damage done by a
broadsword (2d4, d6+1) against the damage done by a scimitar
(d8, d8) there's little difference.  A long sword or elven broadsword
is better than either for base damage.  A silver saber or morning star
is worse than either for base damage.  If you don't mind facing an
orc with a scimitar right now, then Dragonsbane is not any different.
If you are not ready to face an  orc with a scimitar right now, then
Dragonbane isn't going to matter either.

So generally I think it's cool that you found an artifact weapon on the
floor.  Toast that orc remotely as usual with orcs and enjoy the cool
looking expensive loot.

> I did not
> start with the healing or extra healing spells. If I somehow manage to
> slay the hill orc and his 2 buddies, while simultaneously killing the
> 3 soldier ants behind them, is it worth it for my priest to wield and
> use Dragonsbane?

Priests are restricted in all types of edged weapons until given an
edged gift at sacrafice.  Dragonbane is the only unaligned weapon
in the broadsword class.  The only other artifacts in the broadsword
class are Orcrist and Stormbringer and they are only given of you are
chaotic.  If you are not chaotic it is only worth wielding against
dragons.  The question becomes whether it's worth shuttling down to
the levels where dragons are - Both castles and below the Valley of
the Dead.

If you are chaotic your crowning gift is Stormbringer.  That's a more
powerful weapon across the board than Dragonbane.  Since Orcrist
is an elven broadsword it has slightly higher base damage than
Dragonbane and there are more orcs around at the moment than
dragons.  I would even wield Orcrist in preference to Dragonbane
throughout much of the game.

Further, artifact gifts are fooproof every time.  I don't know that
artifacts found on the ground are fooproof.  Long ago they weren't and
I have not checked the core in recent years.  I may well prefer the
blessed fireproof +3 Orcrist to the blessed +3 Dragonbane to the
point I stash Dragonbane and keep Orcrist even once dragons start
appearing.

To me it all adds up this way - Yuo want that artifact, but not as a
weapon to be wielded.  You want it to use in shops with a pet.  Sell
it to the shopkeeper.  Have your pet pick it up and g\bring it to you.
Lather rince repeat and you have all of the shopkeeper's cash a lot
faster than you could using other items.

> With my AC of 0 and only 1 unidentified scroll (the
> only scroll in the game so far), should I just run?

Run based on the crowd of monsters you face not based on the
artifact wielded by one of the monsters.  Run to escape the ants,
killing as you go.  Thin the crowd and make sure you have plenty of
hit points as you go.  If the crowd is gone before you make it to the up
stairs, enjoy the expensive toy for what it's really good for.  If the
crowd is still chasing you when you get to the up stairs, run and heal
then come back and take them out.


